WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.570
[Narrator]:Teenagers are notorious for causing upheaval

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.760
as they stake their ground in social webs.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.480
Turns out, the young of the most&nbsp;massive carnivorous dinosaurs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.920
carved out a vast space for their entire&nbsp;species in prehistoric ecosystems.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.403
Paleontologists have unearthed dinosaur fossils

00:00:19.403 --> 00:00:22.000
that cover an array of species of different sizes.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.939
On a global scale, medium-sized carnivore fossils

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:28.320
are slightly less common than small and large.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.280
Within narrower geographical&nbsp;regions, the disparity is amplified.&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.800
This gap has been a mystery to scientists:&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.360
Did those carnivore fossils fail&nbsp;to survive until modern day,&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.120
or had they simply not planted their&nbsp;
trowels in the right plot of soil?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.573
A new study suggests another answer—

00:00:48.573 --> 00:00:53.350
that carnivorous dinos weighing between 10 and 1000 kilograms

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.190
were replaced by young megatheropods—

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:01.386
hulking carnivores like T. rex that&nbsp;weighed over 1000 kilos fully grown—

00:01:01.386 --> 00:01:04.154
as they developed from football-sized&nbsp;eggs

00:01:04.154 --> 00:01:06.386
into more substantial juveniles

00:01:06.386 --> 00:01:10.000
before eventually filling the&nbsp;shoes of their colossal parents.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.120
The researchers examined 557 dinosaur taxa

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.434
spanning seven continents and 136 million years

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:22.330
across the Jurassic and Cretaceous.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.779
Carnivores weighing between 100 to 300 kilos

00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:30.391
were far less common in local&nbsp;habitats than small and large species.

00:01:30.391 --> 00:01:34.660
It’s as if a mammal community in the&nbsp;modern African Savanna

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.640
had no carnivores between the size of a lion and a bat-eared fox.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.800
The study differed from most dinosaur research&nbsp;
because it looked at ancient ecosystems,&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.640
which are tricky to describe and&nbsp;confirm through fossil evidence.&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.960
So the researchers crafted&nbsp;mathematical models based on biomass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.320
to make predictions about&nbsp;juveniles of particular species.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.280
The models indicated that an enclave&nbsp;
of little giants likely excluded a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.437
more diverse range of species similar in size.

00:02:05.007 --> 00:02:08.410
This dynamic can be found in modern ecosystems:

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.520
when animals have young whose bodies are&nbsp;
extremely small compared to fully grown adults—&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.308
such as egg-laying reptiles like&nbsp;Komodo dragons

00:02:16.308 --> 00:02:20.662
and large crocodiles— they can dominate wide swaths of&nbsp;ecosystems

00:02:20.662 --> 00:02:22.323
as they progress through life,

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.320
shouldering out species that might&nbsp;have otherwise filled those roles.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.000
The findings bolster efforts to understand&nbsp;
how dinosaurs functioned in their habitats.&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.080
New ways of studying microscopic scrapes on&nbsp;animal teeth

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.284
could be applied to dinosaur fossils.

00:02:38.284 --> 00:02:41.204
That would help quantify&nbsp;how dinosaurs hunted—

00:02:41.204 --> 00:02:44.017
rather than typical skull analysis of how they&nbsp;ate—

00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:46.000
to fill additional gaps in knowledge.

00:02:46.905 --> 00:02:48.498
Yet another trail blaze

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:52.550
as we journey&nbsp;to conceive of a land before time.

00:02:54.158 --> 00:02:57.149
[Music]

